{
  "segments": [
    {
      "text": "Waddington-OT 使用时间进程中的单细胞表达谱快照来推断细胞的可能来源与命运。",
      "basis": "KG_GROUNDED",
      "citations": [
        {
          "index": 2,
          "quote": "Here, we describe a conceptual framework, implemented in a method called Waddington-OT, that aims to capture the notion that cells at any time are drawn from a probability distribution in gene-expression space, and each cell has a distribution of both probable origins and probable fates (Figure 1). It uses scRNA-seq data collected across a time-course to infer how these probability distributions evolve over time, by using the mathematical approach of Optimal Transport (OT)."
        }
      ],
      "context_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "text": "该方法要求输入为时间进程中的单细胞表达谱，并需要采样时间元数据。",
      "basis": "KG_GROUNDED",
      "citations": [
        {
          "index": 1,
          "quote": "It uses scRNA-seq data collected across a time-course to infer how these probability distributions evolve over time, by using the mathematical approach of Optimal Transport (OT)."
        }
      ],
      "context_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "text": "你提供的条件包含每个时间点的单细胞表达谱和四个有序时间点，这与方法所需的时间进程表达快照在形式上一致。",
      "basis": "USER_PROVIDED_FACT",
      "citations": [],
      "context_fact_ids": [
        "user:expression_profiles",
        "user:sampling"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "该方法通过计算相邻时间点之间的最优传输耦合，再组合中间时间点的传输映射来推断更长时间间隔的耦合。",
      "basis": "CAUTION_CONTEXT",
      "citations": [
        {
          "index": 4,
          "quote": "Using optimal transport, we calculate couplings between consecutive time points and then infer couplings over longer time-intervals by composing the transport maps between every pair of consecutive intermediate time points."
        }
      ],
      "context_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "text": "提醒：该最优传输计算隐含马尔可夫假设，即细胞命运只取决于当前位置而非历史，且只捕捉分布中随时间变化的分量；这属于模型假设，不代表对实际数据的验证。",
      "basis": "CAUTION_CONTEXT",
      "citations": [
        {
          "index": 4,
          "quote": "The optimal-transport calculation (i) implicitly assumes that a cell’s fate depends on its current position but not on its previous history (i.e., the stochastic process is Markov) and (ii) captures only the time-varying components of the distribution (see Discussion)."
        }
      ],
      "context_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "text": "提醒：不同时间点独立采样会丢失时间点之间的联合分布，因此推断的是概率性时间耦合，而不是对同一批细胞的直接物理谱系追踪。",
      "basis": "CAUTION_CONTEXT",
      "citations": [
        {
          "index": 5,
          "quote": "because different cells are sampled independently at different time points, we lose the joint distribution of expression between pairs of time points, called temporal coupling."
        }
      ],
      "context_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "text": "现有条件在形式上满足时间进程表达快照这一输入要求，但无法据此确认数据质量、时间间隔是否足够短或细胞数量是否足够大，因此不能断言该方法对你的数据一定适用。",
      "basis": "MODEL_KNOWLEDGE",
      "citations": [],
      "context_fact_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "clarification": null
}
